The quotation is about capping ground rents on leasehold properties and transitioning them to peppercorn rents after 40 years. The specific mechanism is a price/rent control on leasehold land tenure — a real estate market regulation.

The primary classification is R3 (Real Estate Markets), as this directly concerns leasehold property arrangements and rent regulation in real estate. A secondary classification of K1 (Basic Areas of Law — property law) is substantively justified since this involves changing the legal terms of leasehold contracts.

